# Security — maximum priority

**Security overrides convenience.** When in doubt, choose the safer option and flag trade-offs to the user.

Full guide: `docs/AGENT_GUIDE.md` § Security · `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` §18 · BACKLOG SEC-001…011

## Non-negotiable

| Area | Rule |
|---|---|
| **Secrets** | Never commit `.env`, keys, JWT secret, connection strings. Service role + SendGrid **only** on Render. Nothing sensitive in Nuxt client bundle. |
| **Multi-tenant** | Every tenant row has `TenantId`. EF global filters + API membership check on **every** protected read/write. |
| **IDOR** | Never authorize from client `tenantId` / slug in body — use JWT user + DB. Verify `resource.TenantId == user.TenantId`. |
| **Auth** | Identity completo + API JWT. Invite-only. Lockout + password policy. Generic login errors (no user enumeration). Short JWT expiry. |
| **Public API** | Only `IsPublished` content. No draft/admin fields in public DTOs. |
| **BFF** | Browser → Nuxt proxy → API (reduces secret exposure and CORS attack surface). |
| **Input** | Validate all write DTOs (length, format). Reject unexpected fields. Parameterized queries only (EF). |
| **Uploads** | API-only; whitelist MIME/extension; max size; path `tenants/{tenantId}/…` server-side. |
| **Errors** | No stack traces or internal details in production responses. |
| **Prod surface** | Disable or protect Swagger in production. |

## Before finishing any feature

- [ ] Cross-tenant access impossible for tenant A → tenant B?
- [ ] Role enforced (`[Authorize(Roles)]` + tenant check)?
- [ ] Secrets only in server env?
- [ ] Public/contact endpoints rate-limited?
- [ ] Security regression test or IT-* isolation test when touching auth/tenant?

## Never do

- Log passwords, tokens, or full JWTs
- Return `"user not found"` vs `"wrong password"` differently on login
- Add `eval`, raw SQL concatenation, or `v-html` with user HTML
- Disable auth/CORS/validation "temporarily" without explicit user approval
- Store uploads on Render disk or accept client-chosen Storage paths

## When adding dependencies

Prefer maintained packages; note if `npm audit` / `dotnet list package --vulnerable` would flag it (SEC-008).
